of you  and we were actually playing on the sort  of the the modern mode gameplay mode  they had the retro mode which actually  brought back the sort of like the  the lives like player lives that you  know every time you die you lose a life  and stuff but  for the modern mode you just go back to  the checkpoint but uh in the top right  corner it sort of keeps track of all the  times like you know you died  it's almost sort of like you know a  puzzle platformer in  a way especially when you work in some  of the new masks uh that this game has  so if we want to talk about those like  talk about the um you know the time  stopping mask for a crash that he uses  and i thought that was a really  unique uh way to you know mix things up  in terms of  you know the puzzle solving there were a  lot of different mechanics tied to  being able to stop time that you know  didn't immediately click with me  at the start but then you know you see  through trial and error you could figure  out how to get through the levels  i got to say it like blended really well  with like the sort of like the core  like you know actual platforming and  jumping mechanics of the game and uh you  know it was pretty interesting seeing  you know uh that that sort of like you  know new  ability being brought in but uh also  there's another one like in the other  level too which was  sort of like this uh sort of like phase  shifting like mask  you click the button to you know  initiate the phase and you know the  world kind of just flips  and yeah you know you see a different  perspective and it you know unlocks  different objectives and  you know kind of going off that in the  um in that dino dash level  um yeah obviously i think i think that  was my favorite of the three that we got  to play  especially because of those you know the  classic crash moments when you're you  know  you're running you know toward the  camera yeah with a dinosaur chasing you  down and you know i mean i  like i didn't i mean it was kind of  difficult to you know get those  uh get the timing and the jumps and the  slides you know try to coordinate all  those in the right way  and then like if you were like  unsuccessful there's some pretty brutal  animations i don't know if this happened  oh yeah yeah when the t-rex eats you  it brought back those like similar  feelings of like you know that sort of  like anxiousness but also that rush  it was a it was really nice to you know  sort of experience that again but like  in a new game  yeah yeah i i think they've done a good  job here at least in the sections which  uh that we played which again you know  our pre-release code um  they've done a good job at you know like  making you know taking crash and  taking its you know foundations in you  know gaming nostalgia and kind of you  know  modernizing it you know we actually also  get to play uh as a  cortex as well you actually revisit past  levels and you know you actually sort of  change the flow of like you know the  events of that level and um  the one level we got to play as him was  actually revisit the first level in the  demo and  uh you actually sort of like alter like  a  an event that happens in that level and  um from there you actually switch back  to crash and you sort of  continue the course of that level but  it's a bit different and it's actually  like way harder too so yeah i mean i  really liked his  you know his special abilities too his  blaster gun and you know the way he  could you know make things into jelly or  you know rock to jump on and  you know going back to your other point  too i thought the way they're  introducing story or you know additional  elements of story in this through that  is very very interesting because in the  dyno dash level too we saw a section  where  you know crash was you know he was saved  by you know by someone but we didn't see  who it was and that's kind of similar to  this  snow way out mission where um you know a  cinematic plays out but you don't have  all the information but then you play as  cortex and you kind of figure out what  happened so i think that's a really  interesting way to deliver story  it was fun to see that sort of like like  that that character brought back again  but also to play as him as well like um  you know then  it's a nice compliment to sort of the  traditional levels too because like  he's not as agile but you know he's got  like other tricks and stuff he can use  so it was pretty it was a nice change of  place  playing as himself yeah it definitely  was like he doesn't have a  he doesn't have a double jump he has a  dash but he doesn't have a double jump  so yeah it's it really creates a  you know fun new way to play it oh  definitely and uh one other thing that's  actually  uh coming to this game as well that we  didn't quite see in the demo but that  coco will actually have more of a  of a presence in this game as well like  him from what i they said um they you  can actually play as coco  in pretty much every crash level uh as  well  so uh that should be uh pretty  interesting like you know just being  able to swap  between the two like you know as you  want i mean something else that we  should probably talk about too is like  the  probably the incredible amount of  replayability you might find in these  levels in terms of you know collecting  all the wimpos and finding all the  easter eggs like  i don't know about you but i didn't get  close to getting you know the hundreds  um in so i could see myself going back  and  you know it would definitely be  challenging but i would love to watch  someone speedrun this game or you know  100  and i think that'd be really fun to see  one thing i will say and um  that you know i really appreciate it's a  really subtle change too but  there's like a circle right underneath  crash  so you can actually see where you're  landing and uh  that wasn't in the original games so  that's like something i really  appreciate because like i think the  challenge that a lot of people face is  like sort of  getting a sense of like you know  distance when you're trying to make the  platforming  like you know like jumps and stuff so um  i i really like some of like the subtle  changes like being added to the game but  which still feel very consistent with  like the original trilogy  yeah i mean in particular there were you  know plenty of platforms i just would  not have made it to if it weren't for  that  for sure yeah all right that's it from  me and alessandro here talking about  crash bandicoot 4. it's about time you  can check out the game for yourself on  october 2nd  for ps4 and xbox one and let us know  what you think of the game in the  comments below  see you next time  you

